   680	impl ChunkData {
   681	    /// Grow this chunk to `total_sections` 16-block sections, padding with air / empty light.
   682	    ///
   683	    /// The chunk-data packet carries no explicit section count: the client reads exactly
   684	    /// `dimension.height / 16` sections, taken from the dimension registry it received at
   685	    /// login. A chunk holding fewer sections than that serializes short, so the client runs
   686	    /// past the end of the buffer and drops the connection with a protocol error.
   687	    ///
   688	    /// Chunks can end up short from two directions: worldgen sizing sections off the noise
   689	    /// generator's `shape.height` (128 for Nether/End) instead of the dimension height (256),
   690	    /// and loading a saved chunk whose file simply does not contain the upper sections - the
   691	    /// on-disk reader derives its section count from the highest `Y` tag present, so any file
   692	    /// written while the first bug was live reloads just as short as it was saved. Padding
   693	    /// here fixes both, and is a no-op when the chunk is already the right size.
   694	    ///
   695	    /// Padding sections are air. Their sky light is `sky_light` - which must be 15 in a
   696	    /// dimension that has sky light, and 0 in one that does not.
   697	    ///
   698	    /// Getting that wrong is not cosmetic. Padded sections sit above every section the chunk
   699	    /// actually stored, and the on-disk reader documents the same invariant: sections above
   700	    /// the highest one carrying a `SkyLight` tag see open sky and are 15. Padding them at 0
   701	    /// instead caps the column with a lid of artificial darkness, and sky light stops
   702	    /// propagating down - which shows up as black caves that snap to full brightness the
