I found one real, live gap: fluid flow currently uses the block-replacement predicate where vanilla calls `FluidState.canBeReplacedWith`. That incorrectly lets low-level lava be replaced by water and does not enforce water’s direction/type rule. I’ll add the state-level predicate, wire it into the existing downward and horizontal flow callers, and test empty/water/lava cases. The other fluid leads are already field/table modeled, renamed, or client-only; the debug function-trace leads have no Rust trace adapter or live command path.
