codex
The live gap is in Shelf’s `setChanged(GameEvent)` path: Pumpkin marks the entity dirty, but its same-state `set_block_state` returns before sending the immediate block-entity update that vanilla performs. I found the existing `World::update_block_entity` path and will wire the shelf caller to it, clearing the deferred dirty flag to avoid a duplicate tick update. Slot’s nine leads all have live Rust equivalents or inline callers, so I will not add dead wrapper methods there.
apply patch
patch: completed
/home/eshanki/pumpkin-wt/loose-coverage-4/crates/pumpkin/src/block/entities/shelf.rs
diff --git a/crates/pumpkin/src/block/entities/shelf.rs b/crates/pumpkin/src/block/entities/shelf.rs
index a90b6290ebb5e2b53eed99eb12537a8a98e158b2..43255952c87ff72606aa33dbf29e62f3b525d0ab
--- a/crates/pumpkin/src/block/entities/shelf.rs
+++ b/crates/pumpkin/src/block/entities/shelf.rs
@@ -144,9 +144,16 @@
             )
             .await;
         }
-        world
-            .set_block_state(&self.position, state_id, BlockFlags::NOTIFY_ALL)
-            .await;
+        // Vanilla `ShelfBlockEntity.setChanged(GameEvent)` sends the block update immediately
+        // (`ShelfBlockEntity.java:87-95`), including when the block state itself is unchanged.
+        if let Some(block_entity) = world.get_block_entity(&self.position) {
+            world.update_block_entity(&block_entity);
+            self.clear_dirty();
+        } else {
+            world
+                .set_block_state(&self.position, state_id, BlockFlags::NOTIFY_ALL)
+                .await;
+        }
     }
 }
 

