     2	//!
     3	//! Ported: the occupant list (`stored`, max 3), `Occupant`'s `ticks_in_hive` /
     4	//! `min_ticks_in_hive` scheduling, `addOccupant`, `releaseOccupant` with its facing/blocked
     5	//! spawn offset, the honey-level growth on `HONEY_DELIVERED` release, `emptyAllLivingFromHive`,
     6	//! `isFireNearby`, `isSedated` and the `serverTick` work sound.
     7	//!
     8	//! Documented reductions, all forced by engine gaps rather than choice:
     9	//!
    10	//! - `Occupant.of` runs the entity through `TagValueOutput` and discards `IGNORED_BEE_TAGS`.
    11	//!   Pumpkin's `NBTStorage::write_nbt` writes a much smaller set, so only the keys that are
    12	//!   actually produced and would be wrong on respawn are stripped (`IGNORED_BEE_TAGS` below).
    13	//! - `EntityType.loadEntityRecursive` + `EntityTypeTags.BEEHIVE_INHABITORS` become a plain
    14	//!   `EntityType::from_name` lookup plus a bee-type check; nothing else can occupy a hive here.
    15	//! - `Occupant.setBeeReleaseData` ages the bee down by `ticks_in_hive` and decays its in-love
    16	//!   timer. Pumpkin's `BeeEntity` carries no age or breeding state yet, so that is not ported.
    17	//! - `EnvironmentAttributes.BEES_STAY_IN_HIVE` (`EnvironmentAttributes.java:150`, raised by
    18	//!   `WeatherAttributes.java:22` and the night keyframes in `Timelines.java:157`) has no
    19	//!   registry here; `bees_stay_in_hive` reproduces it as "night or raining".
    20	//! - `DataComponents.BEES` (`applyImplicitComponents` / `collectImplicitComponents`) needs the
    21	//!   item-component pipeline, so a broken hive does not carry its bees into the dropped item.
